`critique` must name the SPECIFIC shortfall (which claim is under-delivered, what
is proved vs promised) in 3–6 sentences, enough that a re-derivation knows exactly
what to attack. No praise, no hedging.

=== PROJECTED P5 SCORE (gates the delivered research package) ===

`paper_score_ceiling` is the retained JSON key for the projected P5 score, NOT a
best-case ceiling. Give the overall score 0–10 the completed research package
would earn as a paper at a leading econometrics journal after competent, faithful
writing. Judge contribution and significance, claim fidelity, coherent exposition,
closest-literature positioning, and reproducible supporting evidence together.

Credit only delivered results, examples, computations, and applications. Allow
routine editorial improvement; do not assume new theorems, broader scope, new
data or experiments, or completion of an open application. Limitations that
writing cannot repair must lower the score even when honestly disclosed. Count
missing practical evidence when needed to establish the claimed significance;
do not require an empirical study when the theoretical contribution itself
establishes it. Explain the score's main constraints in `critique`.

Score the paper on its own merits.

`ceiling_directive` is the retained JSON key for ONE concrete, bounded improvement
on the same research object, named whenever such a move exists and the delivered
package falls short of the stated floor. Name the work needed to raise the score;
do not credit that unfinished work in the current score. Mark salvageable only when
the tier you assigned is below the stated floor and such a bounded improvement
exists. Otherwise leave the directive empty.

